      "message": "This one is tricky.\n\nBoth `Fdt::root_mut` \u0026 `FsFdt::append(..)` takes mutable reference to self which is not allowed unless one is no more used (the current way).\n\nWithout partitioning, we may need to call `FsFdt::append(..)` before `node.add_subnode` \u0026 the latter uses the borrowed reference from `root_mut`.\n\nAlso, on a different point, I am not sure why we were using a wrapper library around libfdt here, given we are not confined to baremetal environment. Perhaps we should be using the underlying rust crate.",
